    {
      "page_title": "Window Functions: The Big Idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is a window function?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A ==window function== computes a value for each row",
            "It uses a set of related rows: its **window**",
            "Rows are never collapsed; every input row survives",
            "Result: one extra column beside the original data"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Syntax and mechanism",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "function(args) OVER (",
            "  PARTITION BY col   -- groups",
            "  ORDER BY col       -- order",
            "  frame_clause       -- subset",
            ")"
          ],
          "note": "Every part inside OVER is optional"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Empty `OVER ()` means window = the entire result set",
            "Any aggregate (SUM, AVG, COUNT, MIN, MAX) becomes a window function with __OVER__",
            "Details of each clause follow on the next pages"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. GROUP BY vs window",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Feature",
            "GROUP BY",
            "Window"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Rows returned",
              "one per group",
              "**all** input rows"
            ],
            [
              "Detail columns",
              "lost",
              "kept"
            ],
            [
              "Adds",
              "aggregate",
              "new column"
            ],
            [
              "Clause",
              "GROUP BY",
              "OVER (...)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "tables",
          "spec": {
            "tables": [
              {
                "title": "emp",
                "headers": [
                  "name",
